# AppyHour Repository Skills & Knowledge

## Repository Information

### Git Configuration
- **Repository**: https://github.com/ivarhuni/appyhour.git
- **Owner**: ivarhuni
- **Status**: Active git repository with push access
- **Remote**: origin (configured and accessible)
- **Default Branch**: main

### GitHub CLI
- **Installed**: Yes (gh version 2.83.2, released 2025-12-10)
- **Authenticated**: Yes (has push access)
- **Location**: Available in PATH

## Project Structure

### Main Directories
- `app/` - Flutter mobile application
  - `lib/` - Dart source code (presentation, application, domain, infrastructure layers)
  - `android/` - Android-specific configuration
  - `ios/` - iOS-specific configuration
  - `test/` - Unit and widget tests
- `webservice/` - TypeScript web service
- `specs/` - Project specifications and documentation
- `skills/` - AI assistant skill definitions

### Flutter App Structure (Clean Architecture)
- **Domain Layer**: `lib/domain/` - Entities, repositories (interfaces)
- **Application Layer**: `lib/application/` - Business logic (Cubits/BLoCs)
- **Infrastructure Layer**: `lib/infrastructure/` - Data sources, DTOs
- **Presentation Layer**: `lib/presentation/` - UI, widgets, themes

## Development Environment

### Windows-Specific (win32)
- **Shell**: PowerShell (Visual Studio 2022 Developer PowerShell v17.14.3)
- **Path Separator**: Backslash `\`
- **Command Chaining**: Use semicolon `;` NOT `&&` for PowerShell
- **String Pattern Matching**: Use `Select-String` instead of `grep`

### Flutter/Android Build
- **Gradle Properties**: `app/android/gradle.properties`
- **Known Issues**: 
  - Kotlin incremental compilation fails with cross-drive paths (C: vs D:)
  - **Solution**: Added `kotlin.incremental=false` to gradle.properties
- **Build Commands**: Run from `app/` directory
- **Clean Build**: `flutter clean` then `flutter pub get`

### Java/Kotlin Daemon Issues
- If build fails with daemon/cache errors, kill Java processes:
  ```powershell
  taskkill /F /IM java.exe 2>$null
  ```
- Wait 2-3 seconds before rebuilding
- May need to manually remove `app/build` and `app/android/.gradle` directories

## Pull Request Workflow

### Prerequisites (Always True - No Need to Check)
1. ✅ Git repository is initialized
2. ✅ GitHub remote is configured
3. ✅ GitHub CLI (gh) is installed and authenticated
4. ✅ User has push access to repository
5. ✅ PowerShell is the active shell

### Efficient PR Creation & Merge Process

```powershell
# 1. Check current branch and status
git status

# 2. Verify branch is pushed to remote (PowerShell syntax)
git branch -r | Select-String '<branch-name>'

# 3. Check for existing PR (skip if creating new)
gh pr list --head <branch-name>

# 4. Get commit summary for PR description
git log --oneline main..<branch-name>

# 5. Create PR with descriptive title and body
gh pr create --base main --head <branch-name> --title "<Title>" --body "<Description>"

# 6. Check merge status (returns JSON)
gh pr view <pr-number> --json mergeable,mergeStateStatus
# Expected: {"mergeStateStatus":"CLEAN","mergeable":"MERGEABLE"}

# 7. If MERGEABLE, merge and delete branch
gh pr merge <pr-number> --merge --delete-branch

# 8. Verify merge completed
gh pr view <pr-number> --json state,mergedAt,mergedBy
# Expected: {"state":"MERGED", ...}

# 9. Switch to main and pull changes
git checkout main; git pull

# 10. Clean up local branch (optional, ignores errors)
git branch -d <branch-name> 2>$null
```

### PR JSON Fields Reference
Available fields for `gh pr view --json`:
- `state` - PR state (OPEN, MERGED, CLOSED)
- `mergeable` - Can be merged (MERGEABLE, CONFLICTING, UNKNOWN)
- `mergeStateStatus` - Detailed status (CLEAN, DIRTY, UNSTABLE, etc.)
- `mergedAt` - Timestamp when merged
- `mergedBy` - User who merged
- `title`, `body`, `number`, `url`
- `baseRefName`, `headRefName` - Branch names

### Branch Naming Convention
Pattern: `<number>-<descriptive-name>`
Examples:
- `001-csv-pages-automation`
- `002-flutter-mobile-app`
- `003-i18n-image-caching`
- `004-dark-red-ui-revamp`

### Spec Directory Structure
```
specs/<spec-number>-<spec-name>/
  ├── spec.md              # Main specification
  ├── plan.md              # Implementation plan
  ├── tasks.md             # Task breakdown
  ├── checklists/
  │   └── requirements.md  # Requirements checklist
  └── contracts/           # API contracts, schemas
```

## Common Commands & Shortcuts

### Git Operations
```powershell
# Status check (always safe)
git status

# Branch operations
git branch              # List local branches
git branch -r           # List remote branches
git branch -d <name>    # Delete local branch (safe)
git branch -D <name>    # Force delete local branch

# Checkout operations
git checkout <branch>   # Switch branches
git checkout -b <name>  # Create and switch to new branch

# Sync operations
git fetch              # Fetch from remote
git pull               # Pull and merge
git push               # Push to remote
```

### GitHub CLI Operations
```powershell
# PR operations
gh pr list                              # List all PRs
gh pr list --head <branch>              # List PRs for branch
gh pr create [options]                  # Create PR
gh pr view <number>                     # View PR details
gh pr merge <number> [options]          # Merge PR
gh pr status                            # Show PR status

# Useful flags
--json <fields>        # Output as JSON
--base <branch>        # Target branch (usually 'main')
--head <branch>        # Source branch
--title "<text>"       # PR title
--body "<text>"        # PR description
--merge                # Use merge commit (not squash/rebase)
--delete-branch        # Delete branch after merge
```

### Flutter Operations (from app/ directory)
```powershell
# Dependency management
flutter pub get         # Install dependencies
flutter pub upgrade     # Upgrade dependencies
flutter pub outdated    # Check for updates

# Build operations
flutter clean           # Clean build artifacts
flutter run             # Run on connected device
flutter build apk       # Build Android APK
flutter test            # Run tests

# Device management
flutter devices         # List available devices
flutter emulators       # List available emulators
```

## Troubleshooting Quick Reference

### Build Failures
1. **Kotlin compilation errors**: Already fixed with `kotlin.incremental=false`
2. **Gradle daemon issues**: Kill Java processes, clean, rebuild
3. **Dependency issues**: `flutter clean; flutter pub get`
4. **Path too long (Windows)**: Work from shorter paths or use subst

### PR/Git Issues
1. **"not a git repository"**: Already confirmed - not an issue
2. **"permission denied"**: Already authenticated - not an issue
3. **"gh command not found"**: Already installed - not an issue
4. **Merge conflicts**: Check with `gh pr view <n> --json mergeable` before merging

## Best Practices

### Before Creating PR
1. Ensure all commits are pushed: `git status`
2. Verify branch naming follows convention
3. Write descriptive commit messages
4. Check for merge conflicts early

### PR Description Template
```
Implementation of spec <number>: <title>

Key changes:
- <Change 1>
- <Change 2>
- <Change 3>

Testing:
- <Test scenario 1>
- <Test scenario 2>
```

### After Merge
1. Always switch to main and pull: `git checkout main; git pull`
2. Clean up local branches: `git branch -d <old-branch>`
3. Verify working tree is clean: `git status`

## Time-Saving Assumptions

When performing PR operations, you can safely assume:
- ✅ Git is configured correctly
- ✅ GitHub CLI is installed (v2.83.2+)
- ✅ Repository remote is https://github.com/ivarhuni/appyhour.git
- ✅ User has push/merge permissions
- ✅ PowerShell is the shell (use `;` for command chaining)
- ✅ Working directory is D:\dev\appyhour (or subdirectories)

**Do not waste time checking these prerequisites.**

## PowerShell-Specific Notes

### Command Chaining
```powershell
# CORRECT (PowerShell)
cd app; flutter clean; flutter pub get

# WRONG (Bash syntax - will fail)
cd app && flutter clean && flutter pub get
```

### Error Suppression
```powershell
# Suppress stderr
command 2>$null

# Suppress stdout
command >$null

# Suppress both
command >$null 2>&1
```

### String Matching
```powershell
# CORRECT (PowerShell)
git branch -r | Select-String 'pattern'

# WRONG (Bash - not available)
git branch -r | grep 'pattern'
```
